  "query_preview": "..\n/Issued 1248 PM MDT Mon Oct 12 2026/ \n\n - Meteorological Overview:\n\nSome light precipitation is expected over SW MT south of I-90 \nthis afternoon as a weak embedded upper disturbance pivots in on \nthe northeastern side of the upper low centered over Eastern\nOregon. - Moldan/AM\n\nSubtle ridging begins to move in late tonight, which will help clear \nskies a bit. Given recent precipitation the concern will be for both \ncold overnight lows as well as for fog by Tuesday morning in many \nareas. This concern more or less exists Wednesday morning as well, \nthough there will be uncertainty with how much snow pack remains by \nthen.\n\nAfter upper troughing moves across AB/SK Wednesday night into \nThursday an upper level ridge begins to move in. Dry conditions \nremain in place, with highs trending back above average by the \nweekend. -AM\n\n - Forecast Confidence & Scenarios:\n\nDense Fog through Tuesday morning...\n\nRecent snowfall and subsequent melt, light winds, and clearing skies \nwill set the stage for the potential of dense developing from the \nevening hours tonight and persisting through the morning hours on \nTuesday. Latest Hi-Res Ensemble Forecast (HREF) guidance supports \nthe development of fog over the plains of Central and North Central \nMontana and in the valleys of Southwest and Central Montana. \nAdditionally, BUFKIT soundings show saturated low levels beneath mid-\nlevel dry air associated with a region of subsidence moving over the \nNorthern Rockies.\n\nOne limiting factor to the development of dense fog, most notably \nalong the immediate Rocky Mountain Front and Island Ranges of \nCentral Montana will be the direction of surface winds, which will \ngradually turn to the southwest or west. These southwest to west \nsurface winds, even while light in nature, tend to have a \"drying\" \neffect and subsequently limit the development of fog. Given an \noverall favorable setup and support from ensemble guidance thought \nit was best to issue a Dense Fog Advisory from 9PM this evening \nthrough 12PM Tuesday. - Moldan",
